{"assets":["/statement-assets/a9d86a029473a5949338df9880900dde20479d42e183ae9d9fa7d06f17d8b486.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"592","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. The Monster and the Squirrel"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ari the monster always wakes up very early with the first ray of the sun and the first thing she does is feeding her squirrel."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ari draws a regular convex polygon on the floor and numbers it's vertices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1, 2, ..., n"},{"kind":"text","text":" in clockwise order. Then starting from the vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" she draws a ray in the direction of each other vertex. The ray stops when it reaches a vertex or intersects with another ray drawn before. Ari repeats this process for vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2, 3, ..., n"},{"kind":"text","text":" (in this particular order). And then she puts a walnut in each region inside the polygon."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/a9d86a029473a5949338df9880900dde20479d42e183ae9d9fa7d06f17d8b486.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ada the squirrel wants to collect all the walnuts, but she is not allowed to step on the lines drawn by Ari. That means Ada have to perform a small jump if she wants to go from one region to another. Ada can jump from one region P to another region Q if and only if P and Q "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"share a side or a corner"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Assuming that Ada starts from outside of the picture, what is the minimum number of jumps she has to perform in order to collect all the walnuts?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and only line of the input contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 ≤ n ≤ 54321"},{"kind":"text","text":") - the number of vertices of the regular polygon drawn by Ari."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the minimum number of jumps Ada should make to collect all the walnuts. Note, that she "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"doesn't need"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to leave the polygon after."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"9\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One of the possible solutions for the first sample is shown on the picture above."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"592B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/592/problem/B"}